  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Area-Based Intervention for Multi-Sectoral Emergency and Recovery Assistance in Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the face of a multi-faceted crisis context, Mozambique is experiencing high humanitarian needs across the country, particularly in the north where continuous attacks by non-state armed groups have resulted in large-scale displacement and put a strain on increasingly scarce resources and overstretched services. In response to this, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing integrated multisectoral support, considering the whole population &#x2013; including internally displaced persons, returnees and host communities affected by the crisis &#x2013; with a high concentration of needs. Under this grant, IOM is enhancing humanitarian interventions and coordination to strengthen service delivery capacities while simultaneously contributing to the restoration of safe and dignified living conditions for crisis-affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
